
# Right Age to Start Preschool: A Simple Parent Guide

Your neighbour’s child started at two. Your cousin says three is better. The school says “anytime.” So, what is the right age to start preschool?

There is no single age that works for every child. However, parents can look for certain signs of readiness before making this decision. This guide explains what to consider in simple terms.

**Disclosure:** This guide is published by [Thames Valley Preschool](https://thamesvalleyglobal.org/), a preschool brand. The information is general and can help parents evaluate any preschool.

## How Do You Know the Right Age to Start Preschool?

In India, many children start play school between 2 and 3 years of age, while nursery admission commonly begins around age 3.

The right time depends on whether your child feels comfortable spending a few hours away from parents in a safe and supportive environment.

Age alone does not determine readiness. Children develop at different speeds. A confident two-and-a-half-year-old may adjust earlier than a shy three-year-old. Both experiences are normal.

## Key Takeaway

Preschool readiness depends on a child's individual development, emotional comfort, communication, and ability to adjust to a new environment. Parents should consider these factors instead of choosing an admission date based only on age.

